WEBVTT

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:02.345
Detections should be reviewed over time.

00:00:02.345 --> 00:00:06.575
Useful metrics may include alert volume, true positive rate, false positive patterns,

00:00:06.575 --> 00:00:11.070
analyst feedback, coverage relevance, investigation outcomes, and time spent on triage.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.940
Metrics should support decisions.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.670
They help teams identify which detections need tuning, better documentation,

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.720
improved enrichment, or deeper review.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.015
Some detections should be retired because the threat is no longer relevant,

00:00:22.015 --> 00:00:26.203
telemetry changed, another detection replaced it, or the noise outweighs the value.

00:00:26.203 --> 00:00:29.445
Retiring detections is part of maintaining a healthy detection portfolio.

00:00:29.445 --> 00:00:32.880
It keeps the signal set focused, understandable, and useful.
